# ==========================================
# PROJECT-SPECIFIC - sensitive & regenerable data
# ==========================================

# Raw data pulled from Eurostat / Open-Meteo APIs.
# Never committed: it's large, fully regenerable by re-running the
# extraction scripts, and keeping it out of git avoids bloating the
# repo history with binary/JSON blobs that change on every pull.
data/raw/
data/staging/

# Local database files (if you use SQLite/DuckDB for the star schema
# during development instead of a hosted Postgres instance)
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.duckdb

# Any exported dump of the analytics tables - regenerate from the
# pipeline instead of versioning a snapshot
*.dump
*.sql.gz

# Credentials, API keys, tokens, connection strings.
# Even though the APIs used here (Eurostat, Open-Meteo) don't require
# a key today, keep this in place in case you add one later (e.g. a
# paid weather tier, a cloud DB connection string, etc.)
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
config/secrets.yaml
config/secrets.json
*.pem
*.key

# Trained models / large binary artifacts, if you get to a modeling
# stage that serializes objects
*.pkl
*.joblib
models/*.bin

# Personal exploration outputs that aren't meant to be tracked
# (uncomment if scratch outputs start piling up)
# outputs/scratch/

